  "content": [
    {
      "text": "seven ears of corn came up upon one stalk, Gen. 41:5. bore his ear through with an awl, Ex. 21:6 (Deut. 15:17). thou mayest pluck the ears with thine hand, Deut. 23:25. set them to ear his ground, 1 Sam. 8:12. his ears are open unto their cry, Ps. 34:15 (1 Pet. 3:12). They have ears, but they hear not, Ps. 115:6 (135:17; Jer. 5:21; Ezek. 12:2). incline thine ear unto wisdom, Prov. 2:2. stoppeth his ears at the cry of the poor, Prov. 21:13. make their ears heavy, Isa. 6:10.",
